# PART B — FLEET-OWNER-ONLY ACCESS

## 3. REMOVE THE DRIVER APPLICATION COMPLETELY

DriveMitra is exclusively a management platform.

Remove all driver-facing application functionality.

Remove:
- `/driver/*` routes.
- `DriverApp.tsx`.
- Driver login.
- Driver registration.
- Driver authentication.
- Driver mobile cockpit.
- Driver-controlled trip starting and ending.
- Driver-facing fuel entry.
- Driver-facing maintenance reporting.
- Driver-facing alerts.
- Driver-facing service logs.
- Driver application onboarding.
- Driver application navigation.
- Driver-specific authentication permissions.

Remove associated APIs and unused dependencies after checking their relationships with existing production modules.

Do not merely hide these features in the interface. Remove obsolete driver-facing functionality from the application architecture.

### Important distinction

Drivers must remain part of DriveMitra as operational personnel.

Fleet owners must be able to:
- Create driver records.
- Maintain personal and professional information.
- Assign drivers to vehicles.
- Manage licence and identity documentation.
- Track document validity.
- Review trip history.
- Review driving performance.
- Monitor operational incidents.
- Maintain driver assignment history.

Drivers are managed records, not platform users.

**Do not create driver accounts, driver login screens or independent driver access.**

