28. MANDATORY END-TO-END WORKFLOW TESTING
Test the entire system using controlled development/test data.
Workflow A — Vehicle Lifecycle
Create vehicle → Upload documents → Assign driver → Create maintenance schedule → Record inspection → Generate issue → Create work order → Complete repair → Create service record → Update expenses → Generate vehicle report.
Workflow B — Maintenance
Create service schedule → Trigger reminder using test odometer/date → Create maintenance work order → Record labour and parts → Complete service → Update maintenance history → Verify dashboard.
Workflow C — Inventory
Create supplier → Create part → Generate purchase order → Receive partial quantity → Verify inventory → Consume part in work order → Verify stock deduction and audit history.
Workflow D — Fuel
Create fuel transaction → Link vehicle → Record odometer → Calculate distance and efficiency using valid readings → Update fuel expenditure → Generate fuel report.
Workflow E — Trip
Create trip → Assign vehicle and driver → Record route → Receive supported GPS updates → Track journey → Calculate distance and duration → Generate trip report.
Workflow F — Predictive Maintenance
Load sufficient historical test data → Run prediction → Verify supporting records → Display risk and confidence → Generate recommendation → Create authorized issue/work order.
Workflow G — Organization Isolation
Create two test organizations → Add separate vehicles, drivers and financial records → Authenticate separate users → Attempt unauthorized cross-organization access → Verify all unauthorized requests are rejected.
Workflow H — Financial Integrity
Create work order → Attach invoice → Record payable amount → Record partial payment → Verify expense, payable and payment values are distinct → Confirm no duplicate expense posting.
